<title>INDIA: India forex reserves rise to $23.48 bln on Feb 21.</title>
<headline>India forex reserves rise to $23.48 bln on Feb 21.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's foreign exchange reserves rose to $23.48 billion on February 21, 1997 from $23.43 billion the previous week, the Reserve Bank of India said in its weekly statistical supplement on Monday.</p>
<p>	 Foreign exchange reserves (in million U.S. dollars)</p>
<p>					  Feb 21	Feb 14	 Feb 23</p>
<p>					   1997	  1997	   1996</p>
<p>    Foreign currency assets     19,374	19,320	 16,006</p>
<p>    Gold				 4,097	 4,097	  4,587</p>
<p>    SDRs				    11	    11	     50</p>
<p>    Total			     23,482	23,428	 20,643</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
